Third-party code in this folder

engine.js — the fragment shaders of the shot transitions (whip-pan, flash-through-white, chromatic-split,
cinematic-zoom, glitch, light-leak) and the shared GLSL header are ported from HyperFrames,
packages/shader-transitions (https://github.com/heygen-com/hyperframes), Copyright HeyGen,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0).
The caption grouping, timing and entry-move rules follow the HyperFrames embedded-captions skill
(caption-grouping.md, motion-vocabulary.md, rail.md) of the same repository and licence.
Modifications: the shaders run on a WebGL canvas fed by 2D-canvas paintings of two shots of this engine;
the easing curves of the caption moves are approximated by this engine's own easing functions.

investigate.py — the agent loop (one tool call per step, the tool's result fed back as the next observation, errors
as observations, a step limit) and its planning step (a survey of facts given / to look up, then a plan) follow
huggingface/smolagents (https://github.com/huggingface/smolagents, src/smolagents/agents.py and
prompts/toolcalling_agent.yaml); the check that stops an agent repeating the same tool call follows
google-gemini/gemini-cli (packages/core/src/services/loopDetectionService.ts); the rule that search queries are plain
language without operators, and the ranking of sources by who publishes them, follow assafelovic/gpt-researcher
(gpt_researcher/prompts.py). All three are licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. No code was copied; the
logic was written again for this pipeline (JSON steps through ai.py's model rotation, quotes verified in code).

scenes.py / scenes_run.py — the cuts of a clip are found by PySceneDetect (https://github.com/Breakthrough/PySceneDetect,
BSD 3-Clause License, Copyright (C) Brandon Castellano), used as an installed library in the tools' own Python
(pip install scenedetect); none of its code is in this repository. The list of a channel's clips and the download of a
clip are done by yt-dlp (https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp, The Unlicense), called as a program.
